# General project rules

- Stack: Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind v4 + Storybook + Postgres/Drizzle. Keep one coherent Tailwind setup (no duplicate PostCSS / Tailwind configs).
- Target repo: `JustWorks-Digital/citizen-wing-commander`. Do not push scaffolding to unrelated linked clones.
- Prefer small, reusable primitives under `components/ui/` before page-specific markup.
- One-off `/dev/*` preview pages are fine while polishing a UI section; delete them when the review is done. Not required for every tweak.
- Document new standing conventions here or as a new file under `.cursor/rules/`, and link them from `.cursor/rules/README.md`.
- Keep commits reviewable; do not force-push shared history.
- AI agents: keep mid-task progress in gitignored Markdown under `.ai-progress/` (see `ai-progress.mdc`). Never commit those files.
- Follow `naming.mdc` for files, components, DB fields, payloads, tokens, and domain terms (`Session`, `Mission`, `ChecklistItem`, …).
- Abstract API URLs behind named domains in `lib/api/` (see `api-endpoints.mdc`) — no hardcoded `/api/…` or third-party hosts at call sites.
- Keep agent replies very short/concise unless the user asks for detail (see `concise-answers.mdc`).
- On bug fixes for things that already existed or should have worked: 1–2 sentences covering root cause + fix.
- Railway: after a deployable push, watch the deploy and finish production follow-through yourself (see `railway-proactive.mdc`).
